<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 55,576 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 55,576 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 55,576 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 76,238 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	May 11</p>
<p>    Export cargo		11,617	17,784</p>
<p>    Import cargo		43,959	58,454</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, four ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, eight are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     26,246	 Atlas		     12/5</p>
<p>Motor gas	    25,000	 Athenian Harmony	13/5</p>
<p>Crude oil	    50,437	 Johar		     Due</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	  7,000	 Patty Anne		Due</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 Titina		    13/5</p>
<p>Crude oil	    60,000	 Capitan Miranda	 15/5</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
